# What GitHub counts when it draws the language bar.
#
# The bar is by bytes, and this repository holds far more HTML than
# TypeScript -- 284 files against 170 -- because the demos, the kits and the
# editor's fixtures are all written in the language the TypeScript
# implements. Left alone, the bar says "HTML project" about a compiler.
#
# So the examples are marked as what they are. Nothing here is hidden that
# somebody would want counted: `kits/` stays, because a kit is product and it
# is written in Markout on purpose.

# Fragments are HTML with attributes linguist has never heard of.
*.htm linguist-language=HTML

# The demo site: examples of the language, not the implementation of it.
sites/** linguist-documentation

# The editor extension's test fixtures, including the deliberately broken one.
packages/vscode/fixture/** linguist-vendored

# Compiled output that escapes .gitignore.
**/dist/** linguist-generated
